# CoreSystem root .gitignore — one repo covers all 6 planes + verevon frontend.
# Exclude large build artefacts, dependency dirs, and runtime state. Keep
# tracked: source, docs, compose files, Dockerfiles, env templates.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build artefacts
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust
target/
**/target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta

# Go
bin/
**/bin/
**/dist/

# ...but Rust's `src/bin/` is SOURCE, not build output. The `**/bin/` rule above
# (intended for Go/compiled artifacts) silently swallowed every Cargo
# multi-binary source file, while the `[[bin]]` entries in Cargo.toml and the
# `COPY`/`cargo build --bin` lines in the Dockerfiles were committed as normal —
# so a clean checkout could not build the affected crates at all, even though
# `git status` looked clean in a working tree that still had the files.
# A directory must be re-included before anything inside it can be, hence both
# lines. Verify with `git archive HEAD | tar -x`, never `git status`.
!**/src/bin/
!**/src/bin/**

# Next.js / Node
.next/
**/.next/
out/
**/out/
**/node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
.venv/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Generated proto / SDK output
**/gen/cpp/
**/gen/python/_pb2*.py

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor / OS
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.example.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets and local env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Catch every .env variant (including .env.production, .env.staging,
# .env.external-services, .env.zammad — these have been observed to
# contain real DB passwords + integration secrets in this tree). Also
# catch service-named *.env files (apps/Control Plane/lago.env carries
# real openssl-generated keys per its own header).
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
# Track explicitly named template/example variants only.
# NOTE: .env.docker is intentionally NOT tracked — in this tree those files
# carry REAL DB/Twilio/Resend/Google/Microsoft/Okta secrets. Rotate any that
# were ever committed and keep real values in a secret manager.
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.template
!**/.env.sso.template
!**/.env.zammad.example
!**/*.env.example
!**/*.env.template
# Specific known-secret files (defence-in-depth in case the pattern
# above ever loosens by accident).
**/lago.env
**/.env.external-services
**/.env.docker
**/*.env.docker

# Generated runtime key material. Public keys are derived locally alongside
# private keys so the complete trust bundle remains deployment-owned.
**/.secrets/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled Go service binaries (build artifacts — large, non-reproducible,
# may embed baked-in config). A stray `git add -A` committed these; they are
# untracked via `git rm --cached` and ignored here so they don't recur.
# Specific paths (not a glob) so a real `server/` source dir is never ignored.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/Control Plane/org-core/org-core
apps/Control Plane/org-core/server
apps/Control Plane/user-core/user-core
apps/Control Plane/user-core/server

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code agent worktrees — isolated git worktrees (full nested
# checkouts + build artifacts) created for background agents. Never commit.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-machine agent state: local settings, a scheduler lock, and a
# launch.json whose runtimeArgs hardcode this checkout's absolute path. All
# machine-specific. If genuinely shared project config is added here later,
# re-include it explicitly with a `!` rule rather than dropping this one.
.claude/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs and runtime state
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
**/logs/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Coverage and test output
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
**/coverage/
.nyc_output/
**/.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local caches
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pnpm-store/
**/.pnpm-store/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
.cache/
**/.cache/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Legacy nested-repo backups (created on 2026-05-20 when CoreSystem
# absorbed Model Plane + Quarry-v2 into a single root repository). Kept
# on disk in case the pre-root history is ever needed; not part of the
# unified repo.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git.preroot-backup/
**/.git.preroot-backup/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sandbox / scratch
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/tmp/
.scratch/

# Playwright MCP browser-automation artifacts (screenshots/traces).
# Also matched at any depth: these get created next to whichever package the
# run started from, not just at the repo root.
.playwright-mcp/
**/.playwright-mcp/

# Playwright's own run output
test-results/
**/test-results/
playwright-report/
**/playwright-report/
blob-report/
**/blob-report/
.last-run.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc UI screenshots captured while iterating on a design. Real product
# and marketing assets live under a package's own public/ or assets/ dir
# and are NOT covered by these rules — only loose captures dropped at a
# plane or app root.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/Frontend Plane/*.png
apps/Frontend Plane/*.jpg
apps/Frontend Plane/verevonv3/*.png
apps/Frontend Plane/verevonv3/*.jpg
apps/Frontend Plane/verevonv3/apps/*/*.png
apps/Frontend Plane/verevonv3/apps/*/*.jpg
**/image copy*.png
**/screenshot-*.png

# Nested checkout that is its own git repository; `git add` would otherwise
# stage it as a gitlink with none of its contents.
apps/Frontend Plane/agenci/

# Screen recordings + compiled Go migrator binary (build artifacts)
*.mov
apps/Data Plane v2/tools/migrator/migrator

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deployment credentials. These must never be tracked, wherever they land.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEPLOYED_SERVICES_CREDENTIALS.txt
**/DEPLOYED_SERVICES_CREDENTIALS.txt
.env.generated-secrets
**/.env.generated-secrets
